  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAWA: Towards Equitable Access to Quality Education and Health Services in Egypt for Women, Children and Other Members of Migrant and Host Communities in Vulnerable Situations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the framework of the proposed project, supported by the Italian Agency for Development Cooperation (AICS) in Cairo and titled &#x201c;SAWA: Towards equitable access to quality education and health services in Egypt for women, children and other members of migrant and host communities in vulnerable situations &#x201d;, the International Organization for Migration (IOM), Save the Children (SCI) and the Egyptian Red Crescent (ERC) will collaborate and utilize their respective expertise, networks and resources to increase knowledge on women and children&#x2019;s access to education and healthcare in Egypt; help meet the substantial demand for education, with a focus on early childhood education and basic education; enhance access to healthcare assistance, specifically in terms of women&#x2019;s health.</narrative>
  </description>
